-- check/good (core): `suspends` read across two module boundaries
-- (transparent-effects-proposal.md §14.3 rules 3 and 6, §14.6). `Net`
-- declares the primitive; `Users` maps it over a list through `core`'s
-- `List.map`, whose summary makes `fetchAll` suspend; `Page`, which never
-- names `Net`, gets `suspends` from `Users`' record alone. A thunk that
-- would suspend is a pure value to build (`later`), and suspends when it is
-- called (`now`).
pub foreign suspends get : Int → String
